      "writtenOn": "2020-11-16T19:49:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We cannot \"NAK\" VDM:Attention. Thus I suggest this location is inappropriate.\n\nDue to unfortunate quirk of CrOS EC code, this function is handler for both VDM:Status (pre-set HPD) and  VDM:Attention (immediate HPD) which feed into DP \"logical HPD\" queuing mechanism.\n\n[This \"logical HPD queueing\" currently does not exist. Thus we\u0027re not spec compliant. Quirks like this contribute to that. See b/159761215]\n\nThus this would \"terminate flow\" at the VDM:DPStatus message. Not send a NAK; just cease further operations. So \"NAK\" is a bit of a misnomer. (We\u0027re not /sending/ a VDM:NAK.)\n\nInstead I would suggest either:\n(a) not EnterModing in the first place\n(b) being clever [and following spec] by EnterModing but instead PinConfig\u0027ing into \"USB Pin Congiguration\" by honoring the DP VESA spec.\n\n(b) is perfectly allowed and possible. You set bits (1:0) in VDM:Configure to (\"00b \u003d Set configuration for USB.a\") and bits (15:8) to (\"08h \u003d Select Pin Assignment D.d\") or (\"00h \u003d De-select pin assignment.\").\n\nI\u0027m a bit fuzzier on \"USB Configuration\" and \"de-select  pin\", but this would allow us to \"internally track\" logical HPD status of the remote link (see comment above) since we\u0027ve EnterModed and are receiving (VDM:Attention) HPD info. While honoring DP spec by informing the partner we are DP-capable -- but not using it just yet.\n\n(This will shake out a lot of bugs with VESA noncompliant DUT, however. Be warned. It\u0027s like Benson\u0027s dynamic Rp. Yes, it is in-spec, but devices react poorly to it because they\u0027re made poorly.)",
